      "final_answer": "**One documentation inconsistency; no defect found in the constants\u2019 interaction.** Repository untouched.\n\n- **Misleading MD-1 comment** \u2014 `brainspace_copilot_bridge.py:124\u2013126` says MD-1 only adds capabilities. At lines 355\u2013358, a valid score below threshold instead suppresses regex-based retention. Existing tests explicitly require this behavior; the comment should describe MD-1 as authoritative for answered families.\n- `_AGENT_COMMANDS` retains agent tools for leading `/fleet`, `/review`, `/security-review`, and `/research`; `/fleet` also retains SQL. These explicit keeps survive low MD-1 scores.\n- `MD1_THRESHOLD` defaults to `0.5`, uses inclusive `>=`, and accepts environment overrides in `[0, 1]`. Invalid overrides fall back to `0.5`; missing or invalid family scores fall back to regex routing.",
