      "final_answer": "`STARTUP = timedelta(minutes=2)` is a **session-to-launch matching window**, not a subagent/workflow routing threshold.\n\n- At `brainspace_copilot_bridge.py:460\u2013467`, matching requires `launch.start < session.created_at <= min(launch.end, launch.start + STARTUP)`, the same folder, and an unambiguous launch/session pair. Explicit session-ID records bypass this heuristic.\n- At lines 498\u2013505, matched sessions reuse recorded exclusions. New agent/workflow requests can expand availability only with `TOKENMASTER_RESUME_ESCALATE` enabled; otherwise only `TOKENMASTER_KEEP_TOOLS` overrides them.\n- **Boundary limitation:** equal start timestamps or startup exceeding two minutes cause fresh routing rather than reuse. This is deliberate in the current logic, but timestamp rounding could produce a false nonmatch.\n\nNo additional confirmed defect found. Repository untouched.",
